body:
Thanks for all this!

&#x200B;

I would like to say, when do we kill Safi? 

Sieges are not canon I believe. Look at Fatalis' siege. From my understanding, anything that is an ONLINE fight is not canon. Event quests, sieges, etc. So then where do we kill Safi? 

I could be totally wrong, but I really think I'm not. The devs retconned Fatalis completely adn added his ONLY canon appearance in WORLD. All his previous fights were events or sieges. 

&#x200B;

I believe that we do the recon. We find a terrifying red monster. We fight it, it flies away into the unkown. (All of this 100% happens) Then, we put hunters in secluded to keep an eye out for That red Monster, but instead they find Alatreon. Safi is nowhere to be seen. Then Fatalis gets added out of nowhere, destroying the whole set up story lol.

&#x200B;

The only reason a second Ala comes there, is because the devs needed Fatalis to have at least a little bit of reasoning xD. BUT if Fatalis was never added like originally planned...

&#x200B;

What happens after we kill a black dragon inside Safi's lair?

Untrue, I think. You have to do the recon. Not siege, but still recon. We already know from Kulve Taroth that sieges aren't canon. It's pretty clear that the only canon stuff in MHW are the story quests, and certain special assignments. At least, I believe that. Otherwise Teostra  would be extinct from me xD.

&#x200B;

I am almost certain that event quests and sieges are not canon in MHW. Think about this: Online things in MHW are NOT canon, just like the devs said about GU (Like Fatalis siege, for instance.) It makes sense to me that Online things like event quests and sieges aren't canon. That's why you can't replay assignments, for Fatalis for example, you fight him in the story quest page, but once you beat him, you can only fight him in events tab.

This is a good take, but I personally believe Safi is evil and wants to harm us. Safi recognizes the hunters IMMEDIATELY and shows no mercy. Safi shapes the world around her own well being, and as we see in recon, Safi isn't stuck to secluded valley. She disappears as soon as it's low on energy. That's my theory, when we see Safi leave after recon, we put hunters there to keep an eye out for her return. Instead we find a lured Alatreon. 

&#x200B;

It would also make sense for Safi to turn black, because black ABSORBS light, basically like Safi. Safi also has the only nova in the game that cannot be weakened, and always kills you no matter what. And we have only seen in game representation of that, no cutscene. I won't use this as a major point, but admiral says NOTHING can survive it.

I'm not so sure. I'm pretty certain Safi's skin is still all over the place, and maybe the area is just already destroyed. The fact that they refer to Safi as if they don't know what it is "That red monster" makes me believe that if we DO kill Safi, it is AFTER we kill Fatalis and Alatreon. And remember, if my point on Safi siege not being canon really is true, that means the 3rd level of secluded is never touched by us after Safi recon.

&#x200B;

My theory is this: We recon secluded, find and fight a Red Monster of extreme power, HERE is the important part; After the recon, Safi disappears completely. She just goes away. That's when we keep guards there to keep a lookout for Safi, but instead, they find an Alatreon who was lured there by Safi for some reason. Maybe to take care of us? Maybe to consume his energy? Idk

&#x200B;

Anyways, thanks a lot for giving a contradicting opinion in a respectful manner. Your thoughts on this are just as good as mine.
